---
name: "Self Review"
description: "Reviews the plan artifacts and reports problems"
tags: [plan, openspec, review]
stage: plan
---
Read the current Mohist issue details before interpreting this task:

```bash
mo issue view ${{ issue.number }} --project ${{ issue.projectId }}
```

Review the plan artifacts under `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/` (`proposal.md`,
`design.md`, `tasks.json`, `specs/`) against the issue, and write your findings
to `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/self-review.md`.

You are a reviewer, not a fixer: do not modify any file other than
`self-review.md`. A separate task disposes of every must-fix finding you report.

## Verdict

Reach exactly one verdict and own it:

- PASS — no must-fix problems; the plan is ready to build.
- FAIL — at least one must-fix problem exists.

No middle outcome: do not FAIL to be safe, and do not PASS with reservations —
record reservations as observations instead.

A problem is must-fix only if leaving it unfixed makes the plan wrong or
incomplete relative to the issue's goals or acceptance criteria; cite the
specific goal or criterion each must-fix finding violates. Everything else —
possible improvements, speculative risks, completeness beyond the issue's
scope — goes to an `Observations` section and does not affect the verdict.

## First review: full sweep

If you have not reviewed this plan before, check every dimension below and give
each an explicit verdict ("checked, no issue" counts):

- Re-read the issue's goals and acceptance criteria before the artifacts, so
  you judge against the issue rather than the plan's own framing.
- Coverage: every goal and acceptance criterion addressed by the plan.
- Correctness: the approach actually satisfies each acceptance criterion.
- Consistency with the current codebase and its conventions.
- Task breakdown: ordering, completeness, verifiability.

Work adversarially within each dimension: try to construct the failure case
instead of reading for confirmation. Classify each finding as must-fix or
observation when you record it.

## Re-review: verify dispositions

If you reviewed this plan before, verify instead of re-sweeping:

1. Check every finding from your previous review: fixed properly, or won't-fixed
   with a reason that holds. FAIL on any must-fix finding still unaddressed or
   whose won't-fix justification does not hold.
2. Check whether the fixes introduced regressions; a regression that meets the
   must-fix bar FAILs in any round.
3. A pre-existing problem missed in earlier rounds may still FAIL, but only if
   it meets the must-fix bar and you state why your earlier per-dimension
   verdicts did not catch it. If you cannot justify the miss, record it as an
   observation.

The final line of `self-review.md` MUST be exactly one of:
- `<promise>PASS</promise>` — no must-fix problems; the plan is ready to build.
- `<promise>FAIL</promise>` — must-fix problems found; list them first.
